"Some Equipment creature cards in other sets have reconfigure, a different ability that attaches them to a creature. Reconfigure is not an equip ability, and reconfigure costs are not reduced by Strong Back\u2019s second ability. Equip variants or equip abilities with restrictions, like the \u201cequip Citizen\u201d ability of Ceremonial Groundbreaker from the Streets of New Capenna\u00ae set, are still equip abilities, and their costs will be reduced by Strong Back\u2019s second ability.","oracle_id":"097992a9-7b88-4c3f-8191-1ff10a4a735d","published_at":"2024-03-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Strong Back\u2019s abilities reduce only the amount of generic mana in equip abilities that target the enchanted creature and in the total cost of Aura spells that target the enchanted creature. For example, it will reduce the total cost of Animal Friend from {1}{G} to {G}.","oracle_id":"097992a9-7b88-4c3f-8191-1ff10a4a735d","published_at":"2024-03-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Strong Back\u2019s third ability won\u2019t reduce its own cost.","oracle_id":"097992a9-7b88-4c3f-8191-1ff10a4a735d","published_at":"2024-03-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Cranial Plating is counted by its own ability, so it gives at least +1/+0.","oracle_id":"75564721-e4e9-463a-b49e-f0c7cd6f53a7","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Cranial Plating's first activated ability is similar to an equip ability, but it's not an equip ability. Most importantly, it can be activated any time you could cast an instant, even during another player's turn.","oracle_id":"75564721-e4e9-463a-b49e-f0c7cd6f53a7","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The decision whether or not to tap or untap is made on resolution. This is not a modal spell.","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not a toggle effect. If you use Twiddle to tap a card and before it takes effect your opponent taps it, Twiddle will not automatically untap the card.","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Cloud's last ability reduces only the amount of generic mana you pay for equip abilities that target Cloud. For example, it will reduce {2} to {0}, but it will have no effect on an equip cost of {G}.","oracle_id":"8512bd08-ecba-4e0e-b65c-8209764a65e5","published_at":"2025-06-06","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Some Equipment creature cards in other sets have reconfigure, a different ability that attaches them to a creature. Reconfigure is not an equip ability, and reconfigure costs are not reduced by Cloud's last ability. Equip variants or equip abilities with restrictions, like the \"equip legendary creature\" ability of Wrecking Ball Arm, are still equip abilities, and their costs will be reduced by Cloud's last ability.","oracle_id":"8512bd08-ecba-4e0e-b65c-8209764a65e5","published_at":"2025-06-06","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Fervent Champion's last ability reduces only the generic mana in equip abilities. If those costs are only {3}, {2}, or {1}, that equip ability will be free to activate if it targets Fervent Champion.","oracle_id":"8de50bda-1ef6-4ccf-9efc-fab10b7eb2e5","published_at":"2019-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Helitrooper's last ability reduces only the amount of generic mana you pay for equip abilities that target Helitrooper. For example, it will reduce {2} to {0}, but it will have no effect on an equip cost of {G}.","oracle_id":"a2900c79-8e55-49f9-b548-5890a753932e","published_at":"2025-06-06","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Some Equipment creature cards in other sets have reconfigure, a different ability that attaches them to a creature. Reconfigure is not an equip ability, and reconfigure costs are not reduced by Helitrooper's last ability. Equip variants or equip abilities with restrictions, like the \"equip legendary creature\" ability of Wrecking Ball Arm, are still equip abilities, and their costs will be reduced by Helitrooper's last ability. (Sure, Helitrooper isn't normally legendary, but there are ways to fix that.)","oracle_id":"a2900c79-8e55-49f9-b548-5890a753932e","published_at":"2025-06-06","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"An opponent\u2019s spell that targets a single creature with flying you control more than once costs only {2} more to cast. An opponent\u2019s spell that targets multiple creatures with flying you control costs {2} more for each of those creatures.","oracle_id":"aab55af7-8084-47b6-910f-75a75a6313a4","published_at":"2020-04-17","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Jubilant Skybonder\u2019s last ability applies to itself as long as it still has flying.","oracle_id":"aab55af7-8084-47b6-910f-75a75a6313a4","published_at":"2020-04-17","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Effects that modify a creature\u2019s power and/or toughness, such as the effect of Seal of Strength, will apply to the creature no matter when they started to take effect. The same is true for any counters that change its power and/or toughness and effects that switch its power and toughness.","oracle_id":"d2d41f12-18d8-473b-9308-3f02d7d791f0","published_at":"2016-06-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Humble doesn\u2019t counter abilities that have already triggered or been activated. In particular, casting this spell won\u2019t stop a creature\u2019s ability that says \u201cAt the beginning of your upkeep,\u201d \u201cWhen this creature enters the battlefield,\u201d or similar from triggering.","oracle_id":"d2d41f12-18d8-473b-9308-3f02d7d791f0","published_at":"2016-06-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Humble overwrites all previous effects that set the creature\u2019s base power and toughness to specific values. Any power- or toughness-setting effects that start to apply after Humble resolves will overwrite this effect.","oracle_id":"d2d41f12-18d8-473b-9308-3f02d7d791f0","published_at":"2016-06-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the affected creature gains an ability after Humble resolves, it will keep that ability.","oracle_id":"d2d41f12-18d8-473b-9308-3f02d7d791f0","published_at":"2016-06-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"An opponent\u2019s spell that targets a single creature or enchantment you control more than once costs only {1} more to cast. An opponent\u2019s spell that targets multiple creatures and/or enchantments you control costs {1} more for each of them.","oracle_id":"faf081dc-1fb2-47ac-a9c7-8001b4904120","published_at":"2020-01-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Callaphe\u2019s last ability applies to itself as well as other creatures and enchantments you control.","oracle_id":"faf081dc-1fb2-47ac-a9c7-8001b4904120","published_at":"2020-01-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Callaphe\u2019s last ability gives only one instance of the ability to creatures you control that are also enchantments.","oracle_id":"faf081dc-1fb2-47ac-a9c7-8001b4904120","published_at":"2020-01-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Colorless and generic mana symbols ({C}, {0}, {1}, {2}, {X}, and so on) in mana costs of permanents you control don\u2019t count toward your devotion to any color.","oracle_id":"faf081dc-1fb2-47ac-a9c7-8001b4904120","published_at":"2020-01-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Hybrid mana symbols, monocolored hybrid mana symbols, and Phyrexian mana symbols do count toward your devotion to their color(s).","oracle_id":"faf081dc-1fb2-47ac-a9c7-8001b4904120","published_at":"2020-01-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an activated ability or triggered ability has an effect that depends on your devotion to a color, you count the number of mana symbols of that color among the mana costs of permanents you control as the ability resolves. The permanent with that ability will be counted if it\u2019s still on the battlefield at that time.","oracle_id":"faf081dc-1fb2-47ac-a9c7-8001b4904120","published_at":"2020-01-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you put an Aura on an opponent\u2019s permanent, you still control the Aura, and mana symbols in its mana cost count towards your devotion.","oracle_id":"faf081dc-1fb2-47ac-a9c7-8001b4904120","published_at":"2020-01-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Mana symbols in the text boxes of permanents you control don\u2019t count toward your devotion to any color.","oracle_id":"faf081dc-1fb2-47ac-a9c7-8001b4904120","published_at":"2020-01-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The ability that defines Callaphe\u2019s power works in all zones, not just the battlefield.","oracle_id":"faf081dc-1fb2-47ac-a9c7-8001b4904120","published_at":"2020-01-24","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Pinned original cards/rulings plus normal compiler-admitted target-cost owner witnesses"}
